{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJPGTApKEp6kyPa8gkjWFt","type":"tool_result","content":"     159 specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261124T044326Z-restart/review-report.md\n1:# Deep Review Report - mcp-browser-use parent hub (fan-out root)\n5:## 1. Executive Summary\n9:- Counts the verdict used: P0 = 0, P1 = 4, P2 = 17. These are the merged lineage counts from `fanout-merge.cjs`, passed to `review-verdict.cjs` with search debt 0 and no failed required gate.\n11:- Self-check at the root (recorded for the report only, per the fan-out rule): every P1 was re-read against the current tree. All four are confirmed and none changed severity. C2-I1-P1-001 was also reproduced live. `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use --prompt \"debug the 403 Forbidden network requests in chrome devtools\"` returns `\"action\":\"reject\"`. The same prompt without \"Forbidden\" routes to `mcp-chrome-devtools`.\n16:## 2. Planning Trigger\n27:    {\"id\": \"C2-I1-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"file\": \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107\", \"lineage\": \"claude2\"},\n28:    {\"id\": \"R1-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/hub-router.json:98\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"},\n29:    {\"id\": \"R2-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"security\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:46\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"},\n30:    {\"id\": \"R4-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing/README.md:9\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"}\n32:  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\"WS1 routing correctness (C2-I1-P1-001, R1-P1-001)\", \"WS2 Bladebro teardown safety (R2-P1-001)\", \"WS3 stale routing evidence (R4-P1-001)\", \"WS4 P2 advisories\"],\n41:## 3. Active Finding Registry\n43:### P1 (required)\n47:| C2-I1-P1-001 | claude2 | correctness | `010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107` | `evaluateRoute` rejects when the prompt text contains \"forbidden\". Compiled routing is the hub's default and SKILL.md:62 says `reject` refuses, so a 403 Forbidden debugging request is refused. Reproduced live. | Reject on `constraints.has('forbidden')` only. Add a 403 canary that must route to `mcp-chrome-devtools`. |\n48:| R1-P1-001 | vibe | correctness | `hub-router.json:98`, `:119`; `ROUTER.md:51` | Stage two holds \"chrome live manual\" and \"core web vitals\"; stage one `INTENT_SIGNALS.CHROME_DEVTOOLS` holds neither, so a request carrying only one of them never selects the hub. | Add both phrases to `ROUTER.md:51`, or drop them from `hub-router.json`. |\n49:| R2-P1-001 | vibe | security | `mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:46` | `rm -rf ~/.local/state/blade` is unconditional. `install-and-verify.md:77` says to remove the root `bladebro doctor` reports, and only after confirming that no needed named sessions remain. The pass criterion cannot detect a surviving root. | Use the reported root, add the precondition, assert the root is gone. |\n50:| R4-P1-001 | vibe | maintainability | `benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing/README.md:9` | The newest hub-routing record says FAIL with admission exit 1. The holdout gold now expects `defer` and the live admission gate exits 0, and no later run supersedes the record. | Record a superseding run in a new dated folder; leave the historical folder as is. |\n52:### P2 (advisories)\n76:## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n78:1. WS1, routing correctness (P1): C2-I1-P1-001, then R1-P1-001. Rebuild the hub's compiled artifacts and rerun `compiled-route-admission.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use` and the canary fixture.\n79:2. WS2, Bladebro teardown safety (P1): R2-P1-001.\n80:3. WS3, stale routing evidence (P1): R4-P1-001.\n83:## 5. Spec Seed\n90:## 6. Plan Seed\n98:## 7. Traceability Status\n100:### Core Protocols\n104:| `spec_code` (hard) | pass | partial | The forbidden reject contradicts SKILL.md's routing contract (C2-I1-P1-001); the Bladebro update path and run-state prose drift from the shipped state (C2-I2-P2-001, C2-I3-P2-002) |\n107:### Overlay Protocols\n117:## 8. Deferred Items\n124:### Workflow defect (outside this packet)\n128:## Dimension Expansion Map\n132:## 9. Search Ledger\n137:- Ledger note carried from claude2: iteration 5 row SL-005-3 links to C2-I5-P2-001 by mistake; it concerns C2-I1-P1-001.\n139:## 10. Audit Appendix\n147:## 11. Remediation Outcome (after the review)\n151:- **Fixed, P1:** C2-I1-P1-001. The router rejects only on the `forbidden` constraint, and a 403 Forbidden canary failed before the fix and passes after it. R2-P1-001. The teardown reads the root from `bladebro doctor`, waits for the named-session confirmation and asserts the root is gone. R4-P1-001. The new run `benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing--post-review/` records 7 of 7 PASS and supersedes the FAIL record.\n152:- **Downgraded and not changed:** R1-P1-001, now P2. A stage-one replay showed no misroute. \"chrome live manual\" already picks the hub (0.87), and \"core web vitals\" picks sk-code (0.90), whose `WEB_PERF` intent owns it. Declaring \"chrome live manual\" in `ROUTER.md` made an out-of-domain prompt pick the hub (0.835, none before), so the edit was reverted. Dropping both phrases from `hub-router.json` changes the policy hash and is the operator's call.\n1a350b1512b fix(mcp-browser-use): fix the browser hub alignment findings\naf080bb765c docs(mcp-browser-use): explain the bdg dom eval port failure\n3395b32f6b1 fix(sk-doc): accept --reports only for the skill or its hub\n413d3268b8a feat(sk-doc): save mode playbook runs into the owning hub\ne3ca4c96645 docs(skilled): add the results contract to the playbooks that lacked it\na5d1912a6c2 feat(mcp-browser-use): give Bladebro an install guide, manual asset and scripts\n2c87a425e76 docs(mcp-browser-use): record the live Bladebro run and the post-review routing pass\nc7f38f295d2 test(mcp-browser-use): verify the browser hub end to end and close the alignment findings","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:45:46.343Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     159 specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review-archive/20261124T044326Z-restart/review-report.md\n1:# Deep Review Report - mcp-browser-use parent hub (fan-out root)\n5:## 1. Executive Summary\n9:- Counts the verdict used: P0 = 0, P1 = 4, P2 = 17. These are the merged lineage counts from `fanout-merge.cjs`, passed to `review-verdict.cjs` with search debt 0 and no failed required gate.\n11:- Self-check at the root (recorded for the report only, per the fan-out rule): every P1 was re-read against the current tree. All four are confirmed and none changed severity. C2-I1-P1-001 was also reproduced live. `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub mcp-browser-use --prompt \"debug the 403 Forbidden network requests in chrome devtools\"` returns `\"action\":\"reject\"`. The same prompt without \"Forbidden\" routes to `mcp-chrome-devtools`.\n16:## 2. Planning Trigger\n27:    {\"id\": \"C2-I1-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"file\": \".skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/010-mcp-browser-use/lib/router.cjs:107\", \"lineage\": \"claude2\"},\n28:    {\"id\": \"R1-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/hub-router.json:98\", \"lineage\": \"vibe\"},\n29:    {\"id\": \"R2-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"dimension\": \"security\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-da