{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNqp8hec4J27TkTWLvcNbh","type":"tool_result","content":"===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/009-sk-code-browser-evidence\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Make sk-code's frontend verification name the `mcp-browser-use` hub, so a changed page is checked in whichever browser mode the user has installed.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The `sk-code-frontend` row names the hub, not one browser mode, because each user may have a different mode installed. Operator decision on 2026-11-22. It overrides an unverified reviewer suggestion to pin the Chrome DevTools mode. |\n| D2 | The agent uses a browser session it owns. It opens the user's signed-in browser only when the user asks. |\n| D3 | The change is a verification step, not routing. Advisor signals and graph edges stay unchanged. |\n| D4 | A browser run that did not happen is reported as NOT RUN with its reason. It is never dropped silently. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-code` exits 0 and prints 0 warnings\n- [x] `verify-router-sync.cjs` prints `router-sync: 5/5 checks passed` and exits 0\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/009-sk-code-browser-evidence --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub --recursive --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` for every folder it names\n- [x] `check-goal.cjs` prints `RESULT: PASSED` on this packet and on the parent\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/010-mcp-tooling-browser-pointers\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Make every browser pointer in the mcp-tooling modes land on the `mcp-browser-use` hub.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | Generic browser work names the hub, not one mode, because each user may have a different browser mode installed. |\n| D2 | A line about one specific browser names that mode's path inside the hub. |\n| D3 | No tool, program, route or advisor signal changes; only the pointers do. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] The stale-pointer grep in spec.md prints 0 on the working tree\n- [x] `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling` prints `OK` with 0 warnings and exits 0\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub --recursive --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` for every folder\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/011-bdg-eval-port-note\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** An agent that gets `Session target not found` from `bdg dom eval` finds the cause and a working fix in the Chrome DevTools mode's troubleshooting guide.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The note goes in one place, `references/troubleshooting.md` §6, beside the other session errors. |\n| D2 | The note states only what a repro or bdg's source confirms. The theory about where `-p` goes stays out. |\n| D3 | bdg itself is not patched, and other entries in the guide are not edited. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] `rg -c 'Session target not found|returnByValue'` on the guide prints 3\n- [x] `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use` prints `OK` with 0 warnings and exits 0\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub --recursive --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` for every folder\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/012-browser-hub-doc-topic\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** One `/local-doc-alignment mcp-browser-use` run checks every doc that names the browser hub or its modes against the hub's own files.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The topic's code root is the whole hub folder, `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use`. |\n| D2 | The run uses the `devin` lane preset, as the operator asked. |\n| D3 | The run's findings are reported to the operator and not fixed in this phase. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] `doc-alignment.cjs scope --topic mcp-browser-use` prints `STATUS=OK`\n- [x] The `/local-doc-alignment mcp-browser-use --lanes=devin` run folder holds `report.md`\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub --recursive --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` for every folder\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Fix every finding from phase 012's two browser-hub alignment runs, so each command, script and routing claim the hub makes works as written against bdg 0.6.10, Code Mode and the live advisor.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | bdg 0.6.10's installed source is the truth for every bdg command and output shape the docs quote. |\n| D2 | Aside's `examples/repl-evidence-capture.sh` stays open until a live signed-in Aside run can verify it. Its docs are fixed. |\n| D3 | No new feature-catalog leaf for the port defect. The chrome-devtools catalog keeps 31 features. |\n| D4 | Defects outside the topic scope are recorded in `implementation-summary.md`, not fixed here. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] run-probes.cjs on the P03 probe file prints pass=9 fail=0, and advisor_recommend returns no recommendation for \"Inspect the signed-in dashboard and explain the revenue drop.\"\n- [x] rg for a bdg cdp call with positional JSON over the topic scope and the mcp-browser-use hub root prints no match\n- [x] The fixed install.sh finds Chrome on macOS and logs CDP domains available: 53 for bdg 0.6.10\n- [x] The doc-run recheck prints still_open=0, and the skilled-run recheck shows both failing battery rows passing\n- [x] validate.sh --strict --recursive on the hub packet prints RESULT: PASSED for every folder\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:46:36.443Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/009-sk-code-browser-evidence\n## 1. DURABLE DIRECTIVE\n\n**Objective:** Make sk-code's frontend verification name the `mcp-browser-use` hub, so a changed page is checked in whichever browser mode the user has installed.\n\n### Decisions\n\nFrozen choices. Changing one is an amendment.\n\n| ID | Decision |\n|----|----------|\n| D1 | The `sk-code-frontend` row names the hub, not one browser mode, because each user may have a different mode installed. Operator decision on 2026-11-22. It overrides an unverified reviewer suggestion to pin the Chrome DevTools mode. |\n| D2 | The agent uses a browser session it owns. It opens the user's signed-in browser only when the user asks. |\n| D3 | The change is a verification step, not routing. Advisor signals and graph edges stay unchanged. |\n| D4 | A browser run that did not happen is reported as NOT RUN with its reason. It is never dropped silently. |\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## 3. COMPLETION CRITERIA\n\n- [x] `parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-code` exits 0 and prints 0 warnings\n- [x] `verify-router-sync.cjs` prints `router-sync: 5/5 checks passed` and exits 0\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/009-sk-code-browser-evidence --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n- [x] `validate.sh specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub --recursive --strict` prints `RESULT: PASS