{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HMB61qW1rMYjmamW9oH8db","type":"tool_result","content":"--011\n5\n--010 grep\n67:$ git grep -n \"mcp-chrome-devtools\\|mcp-aside-devtools\" HEAD -- .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling ':!*/changelog/*' ':!*/benchmark/*' ':!*.json' | grep -v \"mcp-browser-use/mcp-\" | wc -l\n69:$ git grep -c \"mcp-browser-use\" HEAD -- .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-click-up | wc -l\n120:| REQ-003 | ClickUp names the hub where it chooses a browser | `rg -c 'mcp-browser-use' .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-click-up/references/mcp-tools.md` prints 3 |\n--013 grep\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:59:The browser hub's docs and scripts describe a bdg and a Code Mode that no longer behave that way. Readers copy `bdg cdp` calls with positional JSON, which bdg 0.6.10 rejects. They also copy Code Mode blocks with top-level `await`, which the wrapper refuses, and run `install.sh`, which finds no Chrome on macOS. A request to attach to the operator's own Chrome also routed nowhere.\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:120:| REQ-001 | No doc in scope passes JSON to `bdg cdp` as a positional argument | `rg \"bdg cdp [A-Za-z]+\\.[A-Za-z]+ ['\\\"{]\"` over the topic scope and hub root prints nothing |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:120:| Rescan sweeps over the topic scope and hub root | PASS: no positional `bdg cdp` call, no \"26 tools\", no bdg Node 18 left |\n--009\n193:| `sk-code-frontend` | The changed file checked against `sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md`, which the quality runner names for stylesheet, markup and component files, plus the changed page opened through the `mcp-browser-use` hub in whichever browser mode the user has installed (Chrome DevTools, Aside or Bladebro): a screenshot at the affected viewport and the console showing no new errors, or NOT RUN with the reason, such as no browser mode installed. The agent uses a browser session it owns, and opens the user's signed-in browser only when the user asks. A Figma comparison records the five passes in `sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md` |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:46:41.865Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--011\n5\n--010 grep\n67:$ git grep -n \"mcp-chrome-devtools\\|mcp-aside-devtools\" HEAD -- .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling ':!*/changelog/*' ':!*/benchmark/*' ':!*.json' | grep -v \"mcp-browser-use/mcp-\" | wc -l\n69:$ git grep -c \"mcp-browser-use\" HEAD -- .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-click-up | wc -l\n120:| REQ-003 | ClickUp names the hub where it chooses a browser | `rg -c 'mcp-browser-use' .skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-click-up/references/mcp-tools.md` prints 3 |\n--013 grep\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:59:The browser hub's docs and scripts describe a bdg and a Code Mode that no longer behave that way. Readers copy `bdg cdp` calls with positional JSON, which bdg 0.6.10 rejects. They also copy Code Mode blocks with top-level `await`, which the wrapper refuses, and run `install.sh`, which finds no Chrome on macOS. A request to attach to the operator's own Chrome also routed nowhere.\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/spec.md:120:| REQ-001 | No doc in scope passes JSON to `bdg cdp` as a positional argument | `rg \"bdg cdp [A-Za-z]+\\.[A-Za-z]+ ['\\\"{]\"` over the topic scope and hub root prints nothing |\nspecs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs/implementation-summary.md:120:| Rescan sweeps over the topic scope and hub root | PASS: no positional `bdg cdp` call, no \"26 tools\", no bdg Node 18 left |\n--009\n193:| `sk-code-frontend` | The changed file checked against `sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md`, which the quality runner names for stylesheet, markup and component files, plus the changed page opened through the `mcp-browser-use` hub in whichever browser mode the user has installed (Chrome DevTools, Aside or Bladebro): a screenshot at the affected viewport and the console showing no new errors, or NOT RUN with the reason, such as no browser mode installed. The agent uses a browser session it owns, and opens the user's signed-in browser only when the user asks. A Figma comparison records the five passes in `sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md` |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HMB61qW1rMYjmamW9oH8db","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
