{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017fpb8p1CQJKcbtdnoEB2nq","type":"tool_result","content":"10:    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n86: .../mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh          |   4 +-\n88: .../mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh         |  29 +--\ncommit 1a350b1512bdabbf861d63fe5c1ca2bf343c8522\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<email>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 23 22:56:52 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(mcp-browser-use): fix the browser hub alignment findings\n    \n    The two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects. Docs\n    passed JSON to bdg cdp as a positional argument, which bdg 0.6.10\n    rejects. Code Mode blocks used top-level await, which the wrapper\n    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n    The example scripts never counted console errors.\n    \n    The docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10's source and live Code Mode\n    probes. The advisor lifts its read-only floor for an own-Chrome attach\n    request, so \"attach to my own Chrome and inspect the signed-in\n    dashboard\" reaches Chrome DevTools, while two negative controls stay\n    unrouted. The Devin allowlist gains deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017-max, the\n    freshness panel stops reporting private local-* skills as gone and the\n    v4.2.0.0 release notes name the bdg port defect.\n    \n    Spec: mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs\n    Commit-Id: 0015972\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh\nindex 3ada47d379b..8b1ea3a3dea 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh\n@@ -157,11 +157,11 @@ check_command() {\n }\n \n66:| `mcp-browser-use/benchmark/README.md`, `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Modified | Hub root docs |\n70:| `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` and `tests/scorer/route-gates.vitest.ts` | Modified | Own-Chrome attach lift and its tests |\n73:| `system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`, `tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts` | Modified | Devin model `deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017-max` |\n111:| Advisor suite, `npx vitest run` | `1 failed, 2737 passed, 4 skipped`. Baseline was `1 failed, 2734 passed`. The one failure is the same pre-existing empty `system-skilled-bots` folder |\n114:| `fanout-run.vitest.ts` and `combo-matrix.vitest.ts` | PASS: 244 of 244 and 2 of 2. The new model joined an existing test's list, so the count did not move |\n116:| Freshness panel and its test | PASS: every row `none`, test 19 of 19 |\n120:| Rescan sweeps over the topic scope and hub root | PASS: no positional `bdg cdp` call, no \"26 tools\", no bdg Node 18 left |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:47:32.159Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"10:    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n86: .../mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh          |   4 +-\n88: .../mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/install.sh         |  29 +--\ncommit 1a350b1512bdabbf861d63fe5c1ca2bf343c8522\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<email>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 23 22:56:52 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(mcp-browser-use): fix the browser hub alignment findings\n    \n    The two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects. Docs\n    passed JSON to bdg cdp as a positional argument, which bdg 0.6.10\n    rejects. Code Mode blocks used top-level await, which the wrapper\n    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n    The example scripts never counted console errors.\n    \n    The docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10's source and live Code Mode\n    probes. The advisor lifts its read-only floor for an own-Chrom