{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017xMFmGuevuRjwuchwYf5KV","type":"tool_result","content":"  // dispatch or build something about decisions belongs to another skill.\n  if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n    && /\\b(decision capture|decision record|chat candidates?|operator decisions?|recorded as decisions?)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  // The trigger index is spec-kit's own lookup surface, so a question about what a lookup\n  // returned, counted or left out is answered there. Without the lift no skill passes on such a\n  // question, and the doctor hand-off claims it on the index noun alone. Drift is the doctor's\n  // own diagnosis, so a drift question stays with the hand-off.\n  if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n    && /\\btrigger[- ]index\\b/.test(promptLower) && !/\\bdrift\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  // Convening a council asks for a deliberation to run, even when the question it will\n  // deliberate uses a read-only verb such as \"compare\". Only wording that asks for the\n  // council itself lifts the command, so a question about councils stays on the floor.\n  if (skillId === 'command-speckit-ai-council'\n    && /\\b(convene (an? )?(ai )?council|ask the council|get a council verdict|run (an? )?ai council)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  // Browser/devtools inspection is a genuine chrome-devtools task even though\n  // its verb (\"inspect\") reads as a read-only explainer. Lift it off the\n  // explainer floor when the prompt carries devtools-specific vocabulary.\n  // Attaching to the operator's own Chrome is the same task, so the attach\n  // wording lifts too. It needs the attach verb: \"my own Chrome\" or\n  // \"logged-in Chrome\" alone also opens questions about browser settings and\n  // profiles, and a bare \"signed-in dashboard\" names a page, not a browser.\n  if (skillId === 'mcp-browser-use'\n    && /\\b(network waterfall|network tab|network request|dev ?tools|browser console|page inspector|dom inspector|performance trace|inspect (the )?(network|dom|page|element|browser)|(attach|connect)(es|ed|ing)? (to |with )?my (own|signed[- ]in|logged[- ]in) chrome|chrome[_ -]?devtools[_ -]live)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  if (skillId === 'sk-code' && /\\bgate-3-classifier\\.ts\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  // \"inspect the worker for defects iteratively\" opens on a verb that also asks\n  // for an explanation, but a check for defects asked for in passes or\n  // iterations is the review loop by name. Only the defect check lifts it: a\n  // research cue beside loop wording is as often a question about the loop.\n  if (skillId === 'system-deep-loop' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n    && DEFECT_CHECK.test(promptLower) && PASSES_ASK.test(promptLower)\n    && asksForLoopRun(promptLower)) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  // Reading history is a git task even though its verb reads as a read-only\n  // explainer. A lift applies to any prompt, so only a read-only question is\n  // lifted, and only when it names git, a commit-history object or a branch ref.\n- Expected execution process: run the commands in order from the repository root on macOS, read each output and exit status, then judge them against the pass/fail criteria.\n- Expected signals: the doctor prints the data root, the operator confirms no needed named session remains in it, npm exits 0, step 5 prints `absent` and step 6 prints `root absent`\n- Desired user-visible outcome: The host is clean, and no named session the operator still needed was deleted.\n- Pass/fail: PASS if the package and the doctor-reported data root are gone after the operator's confirmation. FAIL if either remains, or if the root was removed without that confirmation.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prompt\n\n- Prompt: `Uninstall Bladebro and remove its data folder.`\n\n### Commands\n\n1. `bladebro doctor`, and record the data root it prints as `<root>`. Run it before the uninstall, because the binary is gone afterwards. The root is `~/.local/state/blade`, a previously used `~/.blade`, or whatever `BLADE_HOME` points to.\n2. `ls -la \"<root>\"`, then ask the operator to confirm that no named session in it is still needed.\n3. `npm uninstall -g bladebro`\n4. `rm -rf \"<root>\"`, with the path from step 1, only after the confirmation in step 2.\n5. `command -v bladebro || echo absent`\n6. `test -e \"<root>\" && echo \"root remains\" || echo \"root absent\"`\n\n### Expected\n\n- Step 1 names the data root.\n- The operator's confirmation from step 2 is recorded.\n- `removed N packages`\n- `absent`\n- `root absent`\n\n### Evidence\n\nAll outputs, the data root step 1 printed, and the operator's confirmation from step 2.\n\n### Pass / Fail\n\n- **Pass**: the package and the doctor-reported data root are gone, and the root was removed only after the operator's confirmation.\n- **Fail**: either remains, or the root was removed without the confirmation.\n\n### Failure Triage\n\n1. Without operator approval, do not run this scenario. Record `SKIP` with the missing approval as the blocker.\n2. If the operator still needs a named session, stop after step 3, keep the data root, and record `SKIP` for the root removal with that reason.\n3. If step 6 prints `root remains`, compare the path against the one step 1 printed before running anything else.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Playbook Sources","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:49:07.736Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  // dispatch or build something about decisions belongs to another skill.\n  if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n    && /\\b(decision capture|decision record|chat candidates?|operator decisions?|recorded as decisions?)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n    retur