{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RogDN27AuSu7htRS8hHUVS","type":"tool_result","content":"3:description: \"The browser hub's docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10 and Code Mode, and an own-Chrome attach request routes to Chrome DevTools. All 112 alignment findings are fixed or named open.\"\n25:    open_questions: []\n95:| The own-Chrome lift needs an attach verb | \"my own Chrome\" or \"logged-in Chrome\" alone also opens questions about browser settings, and a first draft routed \"Explain what logged-in Chrome profiles sync\" to the hub |\n118:| Skilled-run recheck | Both failing battery rows pass and 4 items resolved. 16 need a reviewer: 15 judgment findings and D-4, a literal fix rewritten to drop a semicolon. D-3 reads as still open only because it was fixed at the predicate |\n119:| Doc-run recheck, run with the skilled `recheck.cjs` | 39 literal findings resolved and 0 still open. 52 need a reviewer: 46 judgment findings and 6 literal fixes later rewritten by hand. `/local-doc-alignment` has no `--recheck` flag |\n126:## Known Limitations\n128:1. **Aside's evidence script is still broken.** `mcp-aside-devtools/examples/repl-evidence-capture.sh` runs its tab and screenshot in two separate `aside repl` processes, so the second starts with `page` null. Its docs (L1-1 and L1-2) are fixed. The script needs a live signed-in Aside run to verify, so it stays open.\n130:3. **Adjacent defects outside the topic scope stay open.** Top-level `await` appears in about 150 lines of docs outside the scope: the `mcp-code-mode` INSTALL-GUIDE, naming-convention, architecture, tool-catalog, workflows, configuration, its other playbook leaves and root playbook (including CM-012's `Promise.all`), `sk-git` references, `mcp-obsidian`, `mcp-click-up`, `mcp-figma` and the Mobbin INSTALL-GUIDE. `assets/config-template.md` still says \"26 tools\". The ids `deepseek-v4-1-flash-high` and `-max` are no longer in `devin models`. Troubleshooting §6 still offers `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED`, and the utcp manuals carry em dashes at lines 36, 45 and 53. The root release notes fail three sentence-length rules that predate this phase, and the advisor suite's one failure comes from an empty `.skilled/skills/system-skilled-bots` folder another session left.\n---\n146:| 006-verification | 007-bladebro-parity-and-changelogs | [Criteria TBD] | [Verification TBD] |\n23:| **Status** | Partial: REQ-002 met 2026-11-21; REQ-003 met at the default threshold but not at `--threshold 0.5`; REQ-008 held only after the browser fixtures were relabeled; REQ-009 not met as written |\n140:| REQ-003 | `mcp-tooling` stops scoring browser requests | The same three requests do not return `mcp-tooling` above threshold |\n149:| REQ-008 | Advisor fixtures still resolve | The golden and labeled fixtures that assert `mcp-chrome-devtools` pass their advisor test run unchanged |\n150:| REQ-009 | Out-of-domain phrases do not route to the hub | One non-browser phrase per new alias does not return `mcp-browser-use` |\n171:| Dependency | Advisor graph rebuild | Old scores keep routing to `mcp-tooling` | Rebuild through `/doctor:skill-advisor`, then replay REQ-001 and REQ-003 |\n47:| **Status** | Partial: REQ-002 met 2026-11-21; REQ-003, REQ-008 and REQ-009 not met as written (see Known Limitations) |\n157:2. **REQ-003 is not met at the specified threshold.** At `--threshold 0.5`, `mcp-tooling` still lists at 0.54 to 0.58 on browser prompts. The advisor maps any nonzero score to about 0.54 confidence, and words such as \"form\" and \"page\" appear in its Notion and Mobbin vocabulary. Supporting evidence only: it is never first, and the default gate (0.8) drops it.\n158:3. **REQ-009 is not met as written.** No out-of-domain phrase picks the hub first, but two still return it. \"set that aside and fix the failing unit test\" and \"write a lighthouse keeper short story\" still list it at 0.82, the band `sk-doc` and `system-spec-kit` share on those prompts.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:50:29.258Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"3:description: \"The browser hub's docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10 and Code Mode, and an own-Chrome attach request routes to Chrome DevTools. All 112 alignment findings are fixed or named open.\"\n25:    open_questions: []\n95:| The own-Chrome lift needs an attach verb | \"my own Chrome\" or \"logged-in Chrome\" alone also opens questions about browser settings, and a first draft routed \"Explain what logged-in Chrome profiles sync\" to the hub |\n118:| Skilled-run recheck | Both failing battery rows pass and 4 items resolved. 16 need a reviewer: 15 judgment findings and D-4, a literal fix rewritten to drop a semicolon. D-3 reads as still open only because it was fixed at the predicate |\n119:| Doc-run recheck, run with the skilled `recheck.cjs` | 39 literal findings resolved and 0 still open. 52 need a reviewer: 46 judgment findings and 6 literal fixes later rewritten by hand. `/local-doc-alignment` has no `--recheck` flag |\n126:## Known Limitations\n128:1. **Aside's evidence script is still broken.** `mcp-aside-devtools/examples/repl-evidence-capture.sh` runs its tab and screenshot in two separate `aside repl` processes, so the second starts with `page` null. Its docs (L1-1 and L1-2) are fixed. The script needs a live signed-in Aside run to verify, so it stays open.\n130:3. **Adjacent defects outside the topic scope stay open.** Top-level `await` appears in about 150 lines of docs outside the scope: the `mcp-code-mode` INSTALL-GUIDE, naming-convention, architecture, tool-catalog, workflows, configuration, its other playbook leaves and root playbook (including CM-012's `Promise.all`), `sk-git` references, `mcp-obsidian`, `mcp-click-up`, `mcp-figma` and the Mobbin INSTALL-GUIDE. `assets/config-template.md` still says \"26 tools\". The ids `deepseek-v4-1-flash-high` and `-max` are no longer in `devi