{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM9nh5bEZnxyHS2LK2Xi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RCcpm2KQaYYBsZYcSTEw1S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; git show --stat=200 1a350b1512b | grep \"mcp-browser-use\" | awk '{print $1}' | awk -F/ '{print $4}' | sort | uniq -c; git show 1a350b1512b -- .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md | sed -n 1,40p","description":"Which packets 013 touched; changelog diff"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":665,"cache_read_input_tokens":177627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":665},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:51:33.395Z","request_id":"<redacted>","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RCcpm2KQaYYBsZYcSTEw1S":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; git show --stat=200 1a350b1512b | grep \"mcp-browser-use\" | awk '{print $1}' | awk -F/ '{print $4}' | sort | uniq -c; git show 1a350b1512b -- .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md | sed -n 1,40p","description":"Which packets 013 touched; changelog diff"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCcpm2KQaYYBsZYcSTEw1S","type":"tool_result","content":"   2 \n  11 001-mcp-browser-use-hub\n   1 benchmark\n   1 manual-testing-playbook\n  21 mcp-aside-devtools\n  36 mcp-chrome-devtools\ncommit 1a350b1512bdabbf861d63fe5c1ca2bf343c8522\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<email>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 23 22:56:52 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(mcp-browser-use): fix the browser hub alignment findings\n    \n    The two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects. Docs\n    passed JSON to bdg cdp as a positional argument, which bdg 0.6.10\n    rejects. Code Mode blocks used top-level await, which the wrapper\n    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n    The example scripts never counted console errors.\n    \n    The docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10's source and live Code Mode\n    probes. The advisor lifts its read-only floor for an own-Chrome attach\n    request, so \"attach to my own Chrome and inspect the signed-in\n    dashboard\" reaches Chrome DevTools, while two negative controls stay\n    unrouted. The Devin allowlist gains deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017-max, the\n    freshness panel stops reporting private local-* skills as gone and the\n    v4.2.0.0 release notes name the bdg port defect.\n    \n    Spec: mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs\n    Commit-Id: 0015972\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\nindex 67cde52d532..ac5b5942766 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n@@ -12,16 +12,16 @@ version: 1.0.27.0\n \n # v1.0.27.0, the dom eval Port Note\n \n-In bdg 0.6.10, `bdg dom eval` only finds the session's tab when the session runs on port 9222. On any other port it exits with code 83 and prints `Session target not found`, even though the tab is open. The troubleshooting guide now names that error and says what to do.\n+bdg 0.6.10 has a port defect in `bdg dom eval` and in the form commands `dom click`, `dom fill`, `dom submit` and `dom pressKey`. They find the session's tab only on port 9222. On any other port they exit with code 83. They print `Session target not found`, yet the tab is still open. The troubleshooting guide now names that error. It also says what to do.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n ## What's New at a Glance\n \n-- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error, its cause and a check for the session's port.\n-- The first fix starts the session without `-p`, so it uses 9222, when that port is free.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:51:34.372Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"   2 \n  11 001-mcp-browser-use-hub\n   1 benchmark\n   1 manual-testing-playbook\n  21 mcp-aside-devtools\n  36 mcp-chrome-devtools\ncommit 1a350b1512bdabbf861d63fe5c1ca2bf343c8522\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<email>>\nDate:   Mon Nov 23 22:56:52 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(mcp-browser-use): fix the browser hub alignment findings\n    \n    The two alignment runs over the browser hub found 112 defects. Docs\n    passed JSON to bdg cdp as a positional argument, which bdg 0.6.10\n    rejects. Code Mode blocks used top-level await, which the wrapper\n    refuses. install.sh found no Chrome on macOS and checked Node 18.\n    The example scripts never counted console errors.\n    \n    The docs and scripts now match bdg 0.6.10's source and live Code Mode\n    probes. The advisor lifts its read-only floor for an own-Chrome attach\n    request, so \"attach to my own Chrome and inspect the signed-in\n    dashboard\" reaches Chrome DevTools, while two negative controls stay\n    unrouted. The Devin allowlist gains deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017-max, the\n    freshness panel stops reporting private local-* skills as gone and the\n    v4.2.0.0 release notes name the bdg port defect.\n    \n    Spec: mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/013-fix-alignment-findings-for-browser-hub-docs\n    Commit-Id: 0015972\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\nindex 67cde52d532..ac5b5942766 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md\n@@ -12,16 +12,16 @@ version: 1.0.27.0\n \n # v1.0.27.0, the dom eval Port Note\n \n-In bdg 0.6.10, `bdg dom eval` only finds the session's tab when the session runs on port 9222. On any other port it exits with code 83 and prints `Session target not found`, even though the tab is open. The troubleshooting guide now names that error and says what to do.\n+bdg 0.6.10 has a port defect in `bdg dom eval` and in the form commands `dom click`, `dom fill`, `dom submit` and `dom pressKey`. They find the session's tab only on port 9222. On any other port they exit with code 83. They print `Session target not found`, yet the tab is still open. The troubleshooting guide now names that error. It also says what to do.\n \n &nbsp;\n \n ## What's New at a Glance\n \n-- A new entry in `references/troubleshooting.md` §6 shows the error, its cause and a check for the session's port.\n-- The first fix starts the session without `-p`, so it uses 9222, when that port is free.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RCcpm2KQaYYBsZYcSTEw1S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
