{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AEXDgZ5jCQ4iyagcAwQgCj","type":"tool_result","content":"53:- The npm package is pinned (`chrome-devtools-mcp@0.26.0` as of this snapshot) — note that `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §4 shows `chrome-devtools-mcp@latest` as the generic install snippet; the live registration pins the version. The live config wins.\n54:- `chrome_devtools_1` and `chrome_devtools_2` carry `--isolated=true` (the parallelism prerequisite). `chrome_devtools_live` carries `--autoConnect` and attaches to the user's own Chrome. All three have an empty `env` (no credentials needed).\n69:          \"chrome-devtools-mcp@0.26.0\",\n93:          \"chrome-devtools-mcp@0.26.0\",\n94:          \"--autoConnect\"\n115:          \"chrome-devtools-mcp@0.26.0\",\n86:`chrome_devtools_live` runs `chrome-devtools-mcp --autoConnect` and attaches to the Chrome the user already has open, with its logins. Use it only for signed-in work that an isolated browser cannot do, such as the ClickUp editor pass, because an isolated instance starts logged out on every run. Aside owns that work by default, and this instance is its fallback.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/assets/utcp-bladebro-manual.md:54:        \"args\": [\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/assets/utcp-aside-manual.md:51:        \"args\": [","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:56:29.895Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"53:- The npm package is pinned (`chrome-devtools-mcp@0.26.0` as of this snapshot) — note that `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §4 shows `chrome-devtools-mcp@latest` as the generic install snippet; the live registration pins the version. The live config wins.\n54:- `chrome_devtools_1` and `chrome_devtools_2` carry `--isolated=true` (the parallelism prerequisite). `chrome_devtools_live` carries `--autoConnect` and attaches to the user's own Chrome. All three have an empty `env` (no cre