{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMAW6hYWMzAJMjs5QDwj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The opus-1 lineage finished all 7 iterations and its synthesis, and its verdict is **FAIL**. There is no P0. The FAIL comes from the workflow's coverage gate: the two required traceability checks still count as incomplete because a real spec mismatch is unresolved. Going by the findings alone, the verdict would have been CONDITIONAL.\n\n```\nBINDING: target=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub\nBINDING: maxIterations=7\nBINDING: convergence=0.1\nBINDING: mode=review\nBINDING: dimensions=correctness,security,traceability,maintainability\nBINDING: specFolder=specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub\n```\n\n**Findings: 0 P0, 1 P1, 8 P2.** It stopped at the 7-iteration cap without converging.\n\n**P1 (the one required fix):** phase 013 raised the Node default from 18 to 20 in one copy of a shared installer helper (`mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:160`) and left the Code Mode copy at 18.\n- A test requires the two copies to be identical, so `node --test .skilled/bin/tests/mcp-installers.test.cjs` now fails (5 tests, 1 fail).\n- That breaks one of phase 003's goal criteria and 013's own requirement that no hub gate regresses. 013's verification never ran this test.\n- The change gains nothing: `install.sh` already passes 20 explicitly. Syncing or reverting one copy fixes it.\n\n**P2 advisories:**\n- Phase 011's recorded check (a match count of 3 in the troubleshooting guide) now prints 5, because 013 added two matching lines.\n- Phases 003 and 004 say Complete, but every goal criterion box is unchecked.\n- The Bladebro installer runs npm install scripts before its SHA-256 check.\n- The Chrome DevTools installer pulls bdg from the floating `@alpha` tag, while the docs are written against 0.6.10.\n- The parent spec's 006 → 007 handoff row still reads `[Criteria TBD]`.\n- The parent's status and progress metadata contradict \"Complete\": `in_progress`, 0% done, next step \"Start 002-hub-scaffold\".\n- 013 changed scripts and docs in two modes without new versions. It rewrote the already-released v1.0.27.0 changelog entry, and Aside got no entry.\n- The Aside playbook has a hand-typed scenario count that the package validator warns about. It is correct today.\n\n**Not re-run here:**\n- The parent goal's stage-one advisor replay (it may write outside the lineage).\n- `validate.sh --recursive` and the doc-alignment scope command (both barred or unchecked in this run).\n\n**Workflow deviations** (also listed in the report's audit appendix):\n- The lineage lock step never ran.\n- I first copied the root config with its `fanout` key and removed it before synthesis.\n- Convergence was only checked from iteration 4 onward.\n- Coverage-graph updates for iterations 1–4 were filled in afterwards.\n- `generate-context.js` was skipped because the dispatch bans it.\n- I wrote one scratch file to `/tmp` and have deleted it.\n\nAll iteration, delta, registry, dashboard, resource-map and report files are inside the lineage folder, and every state record went through the append gateway. The only other changed files under `review/` were written by the fan-out runner. Nothing is the operator's to do for this lineage; the next step is the fan-out merge.\n\nFiles are in `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-1/`:\n- `review-report.md`\n- `iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-007.md`\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opus-1"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":968,"cache_read_input_tokens":248217,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":968},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_